    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\nFixes Qwen3.5/3.6-VL 35B-A3B GB200 SFT failing in the first MoE forward (`Fuse mode requires identical chunk sizes: dispatch=64, combine=128, preprocessing=64`) by turning off HybridEP permute fusion in the GB200 functional defaults.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- `src/megatron/bridge/recipes/qwen_vl/gb200/qwen35_vl.py`: GB200 functional defaults set `moe_permute_fusion_into_hybridep = False`.\n- `tests/unit_tests/recipes/qwen_vl/test_qwen35_vl_recipes.py`: assert the flag is off for GB200 SFT and PEFT.\n\n# Additional Information\n\n- **Root cause:** GB200 SFT inherits the flag from the 16-H100 execution config (`h100/qwen35_vl.py:85`); GB200 `env_vars` set only a 128 combine chunk and never reset it.\n- **Fix choice:** matches GB200 PEFT (flag never set) and GB300 MXFP8 with the same 128/64/64 layout (`gb300/qwen35_vl.py:379`).\n- **Blast radius:** GB200 SFT functional recipe only.\n- **Regression?** Yes — introduced by c94c5b9bb (2026-08-05) H100 exec-config tuning, inherited by the GB200 functional defaults.\n- **Verification:** red-green in `nemo:nightly` (EOS 6437013): RED 2 failed, GREEN 2 passed (file 173 passed). E2E: Qwen3.6 card GB200 SFT, 2x4 GB200 (Lyris 3590126) `HEALTH OK` 100/100 iters, lm loss 2.21 -> 1.03; pre-fix job 3590038 failed.\n- **NVBug:** 7041007.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": null,
